IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch33-38`

-- Tests for chapters 33 to 38.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run; unit ids (33.1, 37.2 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 33 to 38`

§§ `Chapter 33 -- kydells`

-- 33.1: arguments are the kydell is in England, it is upon the sea coast.
#ASSERT `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 34 -- the writ praecipe`

-- 34.1: arguments are the writ is the writ called praecipe, it concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court.
#ASSERT `ch 34 -- the writ praecipe may be issued` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- The text bars praecipe only for such a tenement; for any other the text does not speak.
#ASSERT `ch 34 -- the writ praecipe may be issued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 34 -- the writ praecipe may be issued` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 35 -- measures and weights`

#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `wine` EQUALS `one measure, whose size the text does not state`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `ale` EQUALS `one measure, whose size the text does not state`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `corn` EQUALS `the London quarter`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `cloth, whether dyed, or russet, or halberget` EQUALS `two ells within the selvedges`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `a weight` EQUALS `one weight, whose size the text does not state`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `something else sold` EQUALS `Standard not covered`
-- Arguments are the commodity, the sale is within the realm, the measure used differs from the standard.
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `wine` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `corn` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `wine` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `a weight` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- "throughout our whole realm": outside it the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `wine` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `something else sold` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 36 -- the writ of inquisition of life or limbs`

#ASSERT `ch 36 -- something may be given or taken for the writ` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 36 -- something may be given or taken for the writ` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 36 -- the writ may be denied` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 36 -- the writ may be denied` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 37 -- wardship by reason of a lesser tenure`

-- Arguments are the tenure, what the wardship would be of, he holds also of another lord by knight's service, the fee-farm owes knight's service.
-- 37.1:
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `the heir` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `socage` `the heir` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `burgage` `the heir` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `land of his held of the fief of the other lord by knight's service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Without the second holding the text's condition is not met.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `the heir` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `the heir` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- 37.2: "unless such fee-farm owes knight's service".
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `fee-farm` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `socage` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `socage` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- 37.3:
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `petty serjeanty held of the King by rendering knives, arrows or the like` `the heir` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `petty serjeanty held of the King by rendering knives, arrows or the like` `land of his held of the fief of the other lord by knight's service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `petty serjeanty held of the King by rendering knives, arrows or the like` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `some other tenure` `the heir` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 37 -- we will not have wardship by reason of that tenure` `fee-farm` `the heir` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `have wardship of an heir or land by reason of a fee-farm, socage, burgage or petty serjeanty` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `have wardship of an heir or land by reason of a fee-farm, socage, burgage or petty serjeanty`
#TRACE `ch 37 -- we will not have wardship by reason of that tenure` `petty serjeanty held of the King by rendering knives, arrows or the like` `the heir` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 37 -- we will not have wardship by reason of that tenure` `fee-farm` `the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `have wardship of an heir or land by reason of a fee-farm, socage, burgage or petty serjeanty` AT 2

§§ `Chapter 38 -- putting a man to his law`

-- 38.1: arguments are the officer, credible witnesses are brought for this purpose.
#ASSERT `ch 38 -- the officer may put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth` `a bailiff` FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 38 -- the officer may put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth` `a bailiff` TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- Only a bailiff is named.
#ASSERT `ch 38 -- the officer may put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth` `a sheriff` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 38 -- no bailiff shall put any man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses` `a bailiff` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses`
#TRACE `ch 38 -- no bailiff shall put any man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses` `a bailiff` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 38 -- no bailiff shall put any man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses` `a bailiff` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth, without credible witnesses` AT 2

-- assertions written: 38.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
